From: Protector of Earth Recomp
Subject: [PATCH] VU1 interpreter: FMAC helpers inline, pluggable upper executor, lighter commit

What it is for:
  Translated VU1 code (patches 0018-0019) still paid, per FMAC
  instruction, out-of-line calls into the result and flag model
  (normalizeFmacResult -> calculateFmacExactResult, which decodes the
  upper word again for each lane; updateFmacFlags; ...), and the
  pipeline commit cleared whole queue entries.

The change:
  - broadcast, normalizeResult and the FMAC helpers (applyDest ...
    applyFmacDestAcc) move unchanged to include/runtime/ps2_vu1_fmac_inl.h,
    forced inline (field extractions and lane masks written out).
  - execPairWith(decoded, frame, upper): execPair with the upper
    instruction run by a caller-given function; execPair passes the
    interpreter's own execUpper. VU1NativeAccess::execPairUpper<Fn> and
    VU1NativeAccess::execUpper let translated code build one function per
    distinct upper word and share it between pairs (inlining the whole
    upper executor and FMAC model into every pair made the build about 4
    times longer for the same speed).
  - commitReadyPipelines clears only the valid flag of a committed entry:
    every insert resets the entry or sets every field that is read.
  Same results. Tested: ps2xTest 454/454; the Ben 10 port's 40 captured
  VU1 workloads give the same checksums with and without its translated
  code; callgrind: interpreter 793 M -> 748 M instructions, translated
  code 540 M -> 446 M (Linux, GCC 13).

